Telltale Games has revealed that they're  bringing multiplayer to the upcoming  Batman the telltale series with the new  crowd play feature as reported by shaft  news crowd play was announced at Comic  Con and will allow other players to take  part in the decision-making process the  feature is somewhat similar to the way  games like whiplash handle multiplayer  turning on crowd play will generate a  unique URL that the primary player can  then share with anyone they want to play  with players with the URL will then be  able to open it on their phones or other  devices which will see them added as  participants to the game when the  primary player comes to a choice in  Batman crowd players will vote as to  which choice they think the player  should make the primary player can  enable two modes as to how these votes  will be handled the first will see the  option with the most votes being the  final decision while the second will  display a life percentage of how the  crowd has voted but the decision will  remain completely up to the player crowd  players will also have the ability to  thumbs up or down players decisions in  real-time this obviously sounds like the  perfect tool for streamers but the  developers have noted that the stream  latency could be an issue for live  voting with the thumbs up or down being  the most viable mode at least for the  moment crowd play will be available in  all telltale games going forward  Batman the telltale series will see  players assuming the role of both Bruce  Wayne and Batman in a fresh  interpretation of the universe not tied  to any existing iteration of the  characters the first episode releases on  August 2 and we'll be playing it live so  make sure to swing by GameSpot so we can  all make bad decisions together
 

